---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
---

<Base title="Terms and Conditions — Exporteller">
  <Section class="pt-16 pb-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <span class="inline-block rounded-[var(--radius-sm)] bg-accent-yellow px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-ink">
        Terms of Service
      </span>
      <h1 class="mt-5 text-4xl font-semibold sm:text-5xl">Terms and Conditions</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft">
        Welcome to Exporteller's Terms of Service page. By using our website, you agree
        to comply with the terms and conditions outlined below.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8">
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Services:</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
            Exporteller provides a platform for businesses to connect with
            international buyers and expand their export operations. Our services
            include:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-ink-soft">
            <li>Facilitating communication between buyers and sellers</li>
            <li>Processing payments for orders</li>
            <li>Providing customer support for import or export their services or products.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Communication:</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
            To use our services, you must contact us at
            <a href="mailto:hello@exporteller.com" class="text-brand-700 hover:underline">hello@exporteller.com</a>.
            You agree to provide accurate and complete information and to keep your
            account information up to date. You are responsible for maintaining the
            security of your communications with our team.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Prohibited activities:</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
            You agree not to use our website for any illegal or unauthorized purpose,
            including:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-ink-soft">
            <li>Posting false or misleading information</li>
            <li>Infringing on the intellectual property rights of others</li>
            <li>Harassing or threatening other users</li>
            <li>Engaging in fraudulent activities</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Intellectual property:</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
            All content on our website, including text, images, and logos, is the
            property of Exporteller or its licensors and is protected by copyright and
            other intellectual property laws. You may not use our content without our
            permission.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Limitation of liability:</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
            Exporteller is not liable for any damages resulting from your use of our
            website or services. We are not responsible for the actions of buyers or
            sellers on our platform.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Payments:</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
            As part of our service, we work with Stripe, a third-party payment gateway,
            to process payments securely. Stripe is a trusted and reliable payment
            processor that complies with industry-standard security measures to protect
            your payment information. By using our website and services, you agree to
            Stripe's terms of service and privacy policy. We do not store your payment
            information on our servers, and we are not responsible for any issues that
            may arise from Stripe's services. If you have any questions or concerns
            about payments or Stripe's services, please contact us at
            <a href="mailto:hello@exporteller.com" class="text-brand-700 hover:underline">hello@exporteller.com</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-ink-soft">
            At Exporteller, we strive to provide excellent customer service and ensure
            that our clients receive the best possible experience. Here's how we
            operate:
          </p>
          <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-ink-soft">
            <li>Clients contact us at exporteller.com to discuss their export needs.</li>
            <li>We send an invitation to e-meet via Google Meet to discuss their requirements in detail.</li>
            <li>After reviewing the client's needs, our account managers send a quote detailing services, scope, time of execution, and cost.</li>
            <li>If the client accepts the quote, they must confirm the project with their account manager.</li>
            <li>Once we finish our service, we send a URL so the client can make the payment via Stripe gateway.</li>
            <li>Payments are made once the client receives the service, so there are no refunds available.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Contact us:</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
            We believe in transparency and open communication with our clients. Our
            account managers are always available to answer any questions and provide
            updates on the project's progress. We use Google Meet to ensure that our
            clients have a seamless and efficient experience. If you have any questions
            or concerns about our services, please contact us at
            <a href="mailto:hello@exporteller.com" class="text-brand-700 hover:underline">hello@exporteller.com</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-ink-soft">
            We reserve the right to update these terms of service at any time. Any
            changes will be posted on our website.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
